      "title": "Introduction",
      "gist": "Flexible top-down control of millions of neurons within fractions of a second is too demanding for synapse-based mechanisms alone, motivating a role for brain waves.",
      "question": "Top-down control — why can't synaptic connections alone explain the brain's rapid, flexible coordination? (two reasons)"
    },
