      "title": "20th century neuroscience: The classical model of neural information processing",
      "gist": "The traditional view that each neuron has one fixed, specialized function cannot explain why most prefrontal neurons respond to many different tasks and variables.",
      "question": "Classical connectionism — why can't fixed, single-purpose neurons explain real cortical activity? (counterevidence)",
